## Context
git-erg ticket 0106 renames the `Tags:` header to `Tag:` (singular) to match
the repeatable-header convention (`Blocked-by:` not `Blocked-bys:`). Once that
lands, any IDH skill or script that reads or writes `.erg` files by grepping
for `^Tags:` will silently break.

## Actions
1. Update user-local `erg` binary (`erg update` or rebuild from source).
2. Migrate `~/.claude/tickets/0118-merge-skill-tolerate-plain-ticket-line.erg`:
   change `Tags: needs-human` → `Tag: needs-human` (only IDH ticket using
   the old syntax; confirmed by audit 2026-05-11).
3. Skills/scripts: no work needed (audit returned 0 hits).
4. Re-run `erg validate` on IDH tickets to confirm.

## Was blocked by
git-erg ticket 0106 (PR #122) — landed 2026-05-11. Now unblocked.

## Exit criteria
- No `^Tags:` references remain in IDH skills or scripts.
- IDH tickets use `Tag:` if any had `Tags:`.
- Harness tests pass.
